<title>FRANCE: EU trade must show Africa wheat deals by Dec 11.</title>
<headline>EU trade must show Africa wheat deals by Dec 11.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exporters who have made provisional applications for long-term licences to export European Union wheat to a target group of African nations have until 1500 GMT on December 11 to show their contracts and get their refunds, French grain office ONIC said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The keenly awaited deadline concerns licences valid until June 30, 1997 under so-called Article nine EU rules that require traders to show proof of sale.</p>
<p>The refund for sales to the special group of hard-pressed African nations was set at 28 Ecus per tonne last week, but traders had been left waiting for the contract deadline.  </p>
<p>Traders have made provisional applications to export between 330,000 tonnes and 941,000 tonnes of EU soft wheat to Africa under the long-term scheme.</p>
<p>In France traders bid to export up to 819,000 tonnes of wheat. They applied through the Netherlands to export up to 122,000 tonnes of wheat, EU member country officials said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
